  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.639 acc, while config_003 (rna_only, same RNA settings) achieves only 0.591 acc, confirming that the image modality contributes ~4.8% accuracy. However, we have only tested one image encoder (resnet50) and do not know whether a stronger image representation (imagenet_vit_l) would further improve performance. Question: config_006 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted, multimodal) identical to config_001, cleanly isolating the effect of image representation quality. Why best next: With only two experiments done, the most critical uncertainty is whether the image branch is underutilized. Resolving whether a larger, transformer-based image encoder helps (or hurts) directly informs whether to invest further in image-side complexity (aggregation, fusion) in subsequent experiments, making this the highest-information single-variable test under the limited budget."
}

